/T (4.3 Problem Statement)
/E (4.3 Problem Statement)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
304 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 184 0 R
/E (The main problem addressed in the simulation was the need for a useful and practical Kanban-based productivity feature for freight shippers. The feature needed to support the organisation of tasks across workflow stages and make it easier for users to manage their work. The project therefore required attention to task reordering, movement between workflow stages, and the persistence of task status and priority changes. In addition to the technical side, the project also considered product usage information and user-related feedback so that possible improvements could be based on actual usage and engagement needs.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
305 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 184 0 R
/T (4.4 Project Objectives)
/E (4.4 Project Objectives)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
306 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 184 0 R
/E (The main objective of the project was to design, implement, and evaluate a Kanban-based productivity feature in a startup-style environment. Another objective was to build a task management interface that supported drag-and-drop task reordering and status transitions across workflow stages. The project also aimed to connect the frontend work with a Node.js backend so that task status and priority changes could be persisted consistently across user sessions. A further objective was to use SQL for analysing product usage data, including daily active users and task activity, and then use those observations to suggest data-driven feature ideas. Overall, the project aimed to develop both full-stack development skills and product-thinking skills.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
