720 0 obj
<<
/Title (The expected outcome of the project was a functional and more useful Kanban-style productivity feature for managing tasks in a freight-shipping workflow. Persisting task status and priority changes through the Node.js backend was intended to keep the workflow state consistent across user sessions. The SQL-based analysis was expected to provide a better understanding of product usage through measures such as daily active users and task activity. These observations could then support data-informed recommendations for improving engagement. From a learning perspective, the simulation was also expected to strengthen practical skills in frontend development, React, Node.js, SQL, web development, user analytics, communication, customer support awareness, determination, and product thinking.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 368 0 R
>>
endobj
